===========================================================
CRITERION 7 — FAIL
===========================================================
The settings-manager/handler half of criterion 7 is met (evidence below).
The DISPLAY half is not: the worker changed the CONTRACT of the
`whatif-bigticket-item` template (it now requires the dict
{"Settings":…, "Item":…} and re-scopes with `{{with .Item}}`) and updated
ONE of its TWO call sites. The second call site,
`web/templates/pages/whatif.html:342`, still passes the bare item:

    {{range .Settings.BigTicketItems}}
    {{template "whatif-bigticket-item" .}}          <-- bare item

`web/templates/pages/whatif.html` is NOT in the commit or the manifest.
That call site lives inside `{{define "whatif-results-with-oob"}}` — the
partial `renderRecalc`/`renderWhatIfResults` return from EVERY mutating
what-if handler (internal/handlers/whatif/handlers.go:195 and :446).

PROOF — real handler, real templates, real response body
(probe TestProbeE2EAfterBigTicketExists, setupTestEnvWithRenderer):

  $ go test -count=1 -run TestProbeE2EAfterBigTicketExists -v ./internal/handlers/whatif/
  Error rendering partial whatif-results-with-oob: template:
    bigticket-card.html:31:7: executing "whatif-bigticket-item" at
    <.Item>: can't evaluate field Item in type models.BigTicketItem
  ADD bigticket: status=200 len=118132 hasZebra=false hasISE=true
  ADD onetime (plan now has a big ticket): status=200 len=127688
    body contains "Internal Server Error"          : true
    body contains "Zebra Car"                      : false
    body contains "Zebra Roof"                     : false
    body contains "id=\"onetime-list\" hx-swap-oob" : false
    OOB tail >>>id="bigticket-list" hx-swap-oob="true" class="space-y-2 mb-4">
            Internal Server Error<<<

User-visible consequence, on any plan that has at least one big-ticket
item: every what-if mutation (add/edit/delete an income source, expense,
one-time expense, rate change, …) returns HTTP 200 whose body has the
literal text "Internal Server Error" swapped into #bigticket-list, the
big-ticket items themselves never render, and the response is TRUNCATED
at that point so every later OOB block — including the whole
#onetime-list resync, the very list criterion 7 was about — is silently
dropped from the response.

