`/usr/bin/git show --name-only f479de3 | sort` vs the sorted manifest
.swarm/manifests/RC2.1.files: `diff` produced NO output — the 50-file
commit set EQUALS the manifest exactly. `git status --porcelain` in the
copy is empty, so there is no uncommitted work outside the commit.
.swarm/critical.globs lists `internal/services/retirement/engine/**`;
the ledger row records RC2 as Tier 3 precisely for that reason
("Tier 3: persisted-data change + engine/** critical path"), so the
engine touches are authorised. No file outside the manifest was changed —
the criterion-7 defect is an OMISSION (pages/whatif.html was not
changed and should have been), not an unauthorised change.

===========================================================
OBSERVATIONS (not FAIL)
===========================================================
- Linked-scenario frame: LoadScenarioSettings (settings.go:794) goes
  through decodeSettings, so a linked scenario's LEGACY year keys DO
  convert to months before chain.go rebases — the decode frame matches.
  But resolveCurrentMonth is called only at settings.go:419,
  settings.go:986 and settings_current_month.go:107 — never on a linked
  scenario. A linked scenario with `use_current_month: true` and an older
  persisted start_date therefore keeps offsets anchored to ITS start_date
  while the primary's have been re-anchored to today, and
  prepareChainedSettings rebases by a transitionMonth derived from the
  PRIMARY. Criterion 5 does not require resolving the scenario, and the
  same asymmetry existed before RC2, so this is not a FAIL — but RC2
  makes the frames month-precise and the mismatch is now a whole-month
  error rather than a rounding one. Worth a backlog item / RC3 scope
  question.
- `ExpenseSource.EndMonth` has no `omitempty`, so a perpetual source
  marshals as `"end_month":null` (verified in the marshal probe when the
  pointer is nil elsewhere). Harmless — decode treats a present
  `end_month:null` as nil (probe: `end_month:null present: EndMonth
  nil=true`), so it round-trips — but it does make every saved plan
  carry an explicit null.
- budget_fit.go: inserting scheduleNote between the existing comment
  block ending "(Ruling 2026-08-29b)" and `centsFromDecimalString` left
  that function without its doc comment; the comment now trails
  scheduleNote's. Cosmetic only, no criterion.
- `setupTestEnv` (as opposed to `setupTestEnvWithRenderer`) installs a
  renderer whose responses are JSON, not HTML — verified: the body of
  POST /whatif/bigticket under setupTestEnv contains no "bigticket-list"
  at all. The great majority of internal/handlers/whatif tests use it,
  so that package's suite cannot catch ANY template-contract break. This
  is how the criterion-7 defect passed a green suite, and it is a
  standing blind spot worth a test-only follow-up (V3 pattern).
